  "body": "Hello! I'm wondering, how to set a format for an [input that has type=\"date\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#date-state-%28type=date%29), or [input that has type=\"datetime-local\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#local-date-and-time-state-%28type=datetime-local%29)?\n\nI mean, the \"placeholder\" that I see in Chrome has the format by default: _mm/dd/yyyy_\n\nAnd I couldn't find any documentation about the format for that \"placeholder\".\nI know that out there are tons of [JS-datetime-pickers](https://www.google.ru/?gws_rd=cr,ssl&ei=IVc_V5ffFMiPsgHAnJCgBw#newwindow=1&q=js+datepicker) that solve this task easily. But all those solutions are based on\n`<input type=\"text\" class=\"...\">`\n\nDo you have any plans to improve the standard behavior for `input[type=\"date\"]` and `input[type=\"datetime-local\"]`?\n",
